1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:01,420
You're in space.

2
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:02,610
No suit.

3
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:03,820
Your instinct?

4
00:00:03,820 --> 00:00:05,260
Hold your breath.

5
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:06,233
WRONG.

6
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:07,760
Breathe OUT,

7
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:09,020
with him...

8
00:00:09,668 --> 00:00:10,950
all of it...

9
00:00:11,568 --> 00:00:12,567
now.

10
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,250
Holding it in

11
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:15,033
could tear your lungs.

12
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:17,280
Now, second by second,

13
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:18,940
here's what your body does...

14
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:19,625
and how long

15
00:00:19,625 --> 00:00:21,267
a rescue has.

16
00:00:21,293 --> 00:00:21,793
All he wanted

17
00:00:21,793 --> 00:00:22,433
was a selfie

18
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:24,033
for his niece, Pip.

19
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:24,593
Without the helmet.

20
00:00:24,593 --> 00:00:25,473
"You look like

21
00:00:25,473 --> 00:00:26,803
a goldfish,"

22
00:00:26,803 --> 00:00:27,733
she said.

23
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:28,222
So he pressed

24
00:00:28,222 --> 00:00:29,510
the button marked

25
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:30,910
DEPRESS...

26
00:00:31,046 --> 00:00:32,176
thinking it meant

27
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:33,800
"take the picture."

28
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,030
Second one.

29
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:35,975
Good news:

30
00:00:35,975 --> 00:00:37,200
you don't explode.

31
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,800
That's just the movies.

32
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:39,821
Your skin is

33
00:00:39,821 --> 00:00:41,267
tougher than that.

34
00:00:41,322 --> 00:00:42,442
Second two.

35
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:43,762
The air is gone...

36
00:00:43,762 --> 00:00:45,162
and so is the sound.

37
00:00:45,162 --> 00:00:46,742
The alarm is screaming.

38
00:00:46,862 --> 00:00:47,933
He can't hear a thing.

39
00:00:49,877 --> 00:00:51,090
Is he freezing?

40
00:00:51,090 --> 00:00:51,860
Not yet.

41
00:00:51,860 --> 00:00:53,289
Space is cold,

42
00:00:53,289 --> 00:00:54,180
but empty:

43
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,135
there's nothing to carry

44
00:00:55,135 --> 00:00:56,333
his heat away.

45
00:00:56,390 --> 00:00:58,132
Space is basically...

46
00:00:58,132 --> 00:01:00,010
a giant thermos.

47
00:01:00,085 --> 00:01:01,100
But his spit?

48
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:01,623
Touch your tongue

49
00:01:01,623 --> 00:01:02,610
to your lip.

50
00:01:02,610 --> 00:01:03,280
Feel that?

51
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,350
Second five:

52
00:01:04,350 --> 00:01:05,967
his is boiling.

53
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:06,766
With no air

54
00:01:06,766 --> 00:01:07,830
pressing on it,

55
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:08,647
water boils

56
00:01:08,647 --> 00:01:10,250
at body temperature.

57
00:01:10,250 --> 00:01:11,210
His spit.

58
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:12,386
His tears.

59
00:01:12,386 --> 00:01:13,580
And all that boiling

60
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:14,813
steals heat...

61
00:01:14,813 --> 00:01:16,540
so his mouth gets cold.

62
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:18,300
Almost freezing.

63
00:01:18,326 --> 00:01:19,386
Second ten.

64
00:01:19,386 --> 00:01:20,006
The real danger

65
00:01:20,006 --> 00:01:21,586
is in here.

66
00:01:21,586 --> 00:01:22,786
His lungs are empty,

67
00:01:22,786 --> 00:01:23,386
so the oxygen

68
00:01:23,386 --> 00:01:24,146
in his blood

69
00:01:24,146 --> 00:01:25,686
pours OUT...

70
00:01:25,686 --> 00:01:26,806
the wrong way.

71
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:28,008
And that blood,

72
00:01:28,008 --> 00:01:28,659
with almost

73
00:01:28,659 --> 00:01:30,140
nothing left in it,

74
00:01:30,140 --> 00:01:30,989
is on its way

75
00:01:30,989 --> 00:01:32,400
to his brain.

76
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:33,960
Fourteen...

77
00:01:35,065 --> 00:01:36,350
fifteen...

78
00:01:37,271 --> 00:01:37,967
lights out.

79
00:01:39,510 --> 00:01:40,380
He's out.

80
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:41,740
Not dead...

81
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:42,440
out.

82
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:43,620
And now,

83
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:45,420
a different clock starts.

84
00:01:45,629 --> 00:01:46,189
Ball,

85
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:47,419
the camera drone,

86
00:01:47,419 --> 00:01:48,669
wants to help.

87
00:01:48,869 --> 00:01:49,269
But its fans

88
00:01:49,229 --> 00:01:49,889
need air

89
00:01:49,889 --> 00:01:51,229
to push against.

90
00:01:51,389 --> 00:01:52,349
Right now,

91
00:01:52,349 --> 00:01:53,699
Ball is just...

92
00:01:53,699 --> 00:01:54,549
a ball.

93
00:01:54,884 --> 00:01:55,764
Down the hall,

94
00:01:55,764 --> 00:01:56,524
the alarm reaches

95
00:01:56,524 --> 00:01:57,794
his big sister,

96
00:01:57,794 --> 00:01:58,644
the commander.

97
00:01:59,084 --> 00:02:00,004
She's been rescuing him

98
00:02:00,004 --> 00:02:01,344
since he was four.

99
00:02:01,531 --> 00:02:02,636
Second twenty.

100
00:02:02,636 --> 00:02:03,660
The water in his body

101
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:05,160
is turning to gas.

102
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,300
He's swelling...

103
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,867
like his bag of chips.

104
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:09,527
Pinch the skin

105
00:02:09,527 --> 00:02:11,000
on the back of your hand.

106
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,820
Let go.

107
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:12,625
It snaps back,

108
00:02:12,625 --> 00:02:13,110
right?

109
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:13,811
That's what's

110
00:02:13,811 --> 00:02:15,433
holding him together.

111
00:02:15,460 --> 00:02:16,840
In 1960,

112
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:17,536
a pilot named

113
00:02:17,536 --> 00:02:18,428
Joe Kittinger

114
00:02:18,428 --> 00:02:19,228
rode a balloon

115
00:02:19,228 --> 00:02:21,133
nineteen miles up.

116
00:02:21,170 --> 00:02:21,940
One of his gloves

117
00:02:21,940 --> 00:02:22,976
failed.

118
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:24,160
His hand swelled

119
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:26,133
to twice its size...

120
00:02:26,190 --> 00:02:26,997
and three hours

121
00:02:26,997 --> 00:02:28,180
after he landed,

122
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:29,967
the swelling was gone.

123
00:02:30,015 --> 00:02:31,195
Second thirty.

124
00:02:31,215 --> 00:02:31,615
What does this

125
00:02:31,535 --> 00:02:32,755
feel like?

126
00:02:32,755 --> 00:02:33,995
One man knows.

127
00:02:34,375 --> 00:02:35,895
In 1966,

128
00:02:35,975 --> 00:02:36,535
Jim LeBlanc

129
00:02:36,535 --> 00:02:37,775
was testing a spacesuit

130
00:02:37,775 --> 00:02:38,295
in a NASA

131
00:02:38,295 --> 00:02:39,755
vacuum chamber,

132
00:02:39,755 --> 00:02:40,495
when its air hose

133
00:02:40,495 --> 00:02:41,595
came loose.

134
00:02:41,801 --> 00:02:42,281
He stayed awake

135
00:02:42,281 --> 00:02:42,761
for about

136
00:02:42,761 --> 00:02:44,321
fourteen seconds.

137
00:02:44,381 --> 00:02:44,841
The last thing

138
00:02:44,841 --> 00:02:45,781
he remembered?

139
00:02:45,901 --> 00:02:47,421
The spit on his tongue...

140
00:02:47,421 --> 00:02:48,721
starting to bubble.

141
00:02:48,908 --> 00:02:49,628
They pumped the air

142
00:02:49,628 --> 00:02:50,618
back in,

143
00:02:50,618 --> 00:02:51,488
fast.

144
00:02:51,488 --> 00:02:52,628
And he was fine.

145
00:02:52,628 --> 00:02:53,388
He just couldn't

146
00:02:53,388 --> 00:02:54,388
taste much...

147
00:02:54,388 --> 00:02:55,688
for four days.

148
00:02:56,127 --> 00:02:57,810
Second forty-five.

149
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:58,767
Every bit of gas

150
00:02:58,767 --> 00:02:59,410
in his gut

151
00:02:59,410 --> 00:03:01,080
is swelling too.

152
00:03:01,877 --> 00:03:02,430
Yes.

153
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:03,907
That gas.

154
00:03:04,027 --> 00:03:05,315
Second sixty.

155
00:03:05,315 --> 00:03:05,931
His heart

156
00:03:05,931 --> 00:03:07,170
is still beating...

157
00:03:07,170 --> 00:03:08,170
but slower,

158
00:03:08,170 --> 00:03:09,400
and slower.

159
00:03:09,424 --> 00:03:09,894
So how long

160
00:03:09,894 --> 00:03:10,974
does he have?

161
00:03:11,074 --> 00:03:11,474
Nobody's allowed

162
00:03:11,414 --> 00:03:11,994
to test that

163
00:03:11,994 --> 00:03:13,034
on a person.

164
00:03:13,274 --> 00:03:14,254
In the nineteen-sixties,

165
00:03:14,254 --> 00:03:15,054
they tested it

166
00:03:15,054 --> 00:03:16,134
on animals.

167
00:03:16,390 --> 00:03:16,968
Every dog

168
00:03:16,968 --> 00:03:17,600
brought back

169
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,270
within ninety seconds

170
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:20,050
lived.

171
00:03:20,050 --> 00:03:20,650
After about

172
00:03:20,650 --> 00:03:21,739
three minutes...

173
00:03:21,739 --> 00:03:23,067
most didn't.

174
00:03:23,108 --> 00:03:24,648
In 1971,

175
00:03:24,958 --> 00:03:25,788
a valve opened

176
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:27,348
on a Soyuz capsule,

177
00:03:27,488 --> 00:03:28,708
on its way home.

178
00:03:29,028 --> 00:03:29,968
Its three cosmonauts

179
00:03:29,968 --> 00:03:31,788
are still the only people

180
00:03:31,788 --> 00:03:32,988
who ever died

181
00:03:32,988 --> 00:03:34,208
in space.

182
00:03:34,802 --> 00:03:36,142
Second eighty.

183
00:03:36,462 --> 00:03:36,862
Her hand

184
00:03:36,742 --> 00:03:38,367
hits REPRESS.

185
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:42,647
Second ninety.

186
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:44,080
Air.

187
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:45,410
And like

188
00:03:45,410 --> 00:03:46,930
Jim LeBlanc...

189
00:03:47,190 --> 00:03:48,490
he wakes up.

190
00:03:48,942 --> 00:03:50,172
Hold out your hand.

191
00:03:50,172 --> 00:03:50,812
Right now,

192
00:03:50,812 --> 00:03:52,132
the air is pressing on it

193
00:03:52,132 --> 00:03:52,632
with the weight

194
00:03:52,632 --> 00:03:53,852
of a grown-up.

195
00:03:53,852 --> 00:03:54,942
You don't feel it,

196
00:03:54,942 --> 00:03:55,532
because your body

197
00:03:55,532 --> 00:03:56,152
pushes back

198
00:03:56,152 --> 00:03:57,572
just as hard.

199
00:03:57,660 --> 00:03:58,490
Space doesn't

200
00:03:58,490 --> 00:03:59,645
pull you apart.

201
00:03:59,645 --> 00:04:00,445
It just stops

202
00:04:00,445 --> 00:04:02,130
holding you together.

203
00:04:02,266 --> 00:04:02,869
He was puffy

204
00:04:02,869 --> 00:04:04,260
for a couple of days.

205
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:05,191
His pride...

206
00:04:05,191 --> 00:04:06,667
a lot longer.

207
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:07,300
So:

208
00:04:07,300 --> 00:04:08,550
one more selfie.

209
00:04:08,550 --> 00:04:09,420
Helmet on.

210
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:10,253
Goldfish bowl

211
00:04:10,253 --> 00:04:11,500
and all.

212
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:13,010
Turns out...

213
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:13,704
we all live

214
00:04:13,704 --> 00:04:15,484
in a goldfish bowl.

215
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:16,904
Ours is just

216
00:04:16,904 --> 00:04:18,340
very big...

217
00:04:18,410 --> 00:04:20,000
and very thin.

218
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,620
Next week:

219
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:24,703
what happens if you

220
00:04:24,703 --> 00:04:26,980
stop brushing your teeth.

221
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:27,970
Subscribe...

222
00:04:27,970 --> 00:04:28,370
and keep

223
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:29,708
your helmet on.

